    "topic_title": "Trigonometric Equations and Inequalities",
    "stem": "Which set contains all solutions to sin x = −1/2 on the interval 0 ≤ x < 4π?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "{7π/6, 11π/6, 19π/6, 23π/6}",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "The reference angle is π/6, and sine is negative in Quadrants III and IV, giving 7π/6 and 11π/6 in the first cycle. Adding the period 2π to each gives 19π/6 and 23π/6, completing the solutions in the stated interval."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "{7π/6, 11π/6}",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "First-cycle-only error: These are both solutions in 0 ≤ x < 2π, but the stated interval includes a second complete cycle. The solutions obtained by adding 2π are missing. Fix: Add 2π to each solution and check whether it remains in the interval."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "{7π/6, 19π/6}",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Missing-quadrant error: This set repeats the Quadrant III solution but omits the Quadrant IV solution in each cycle. Sine is negative in both quadrants, so one solution per cycle is insufficient. Fix: Identify both quadrants where sine is negative before generating repeated solutions."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "{π/6, 5π/6, 13π/6, 17π/6}",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Sign error: These angles have sine equal to 1/2, not −1/2. The reference angle is appropriate, but Quadrants I and II give the wrong sign. Fix: Check the sine sign in each chosen quadrant against the equation."
     }
    ]
   },
